  "result": "I found the cause and wrote a fix plan. The plan-approval tool isn't available in this session, so here it is for you to review. Nothing has been changed yet.\n\n**Cause:** In `src/click/core.py:392`, when a subcommand's context is created, it copies the parent's whole `default_map` instead of taking the part filed under its own name:\n\n```python\ndefault_map = parent.default_map          # current (wrong)\ndefault_map = parent.default_map.get(info_name)   # fix\n```\n\nSo with `default_map={\"sub\": {\"opt\": 42}}`, the `sub` command looks for `\"opt\"` at the top level, doesn't find it, and uses the option's built-in default instead. The one-line fix matches how upstream Click does it. If a subcommand has no entry in the map, it gets no map defaults.\n\n**Tests to add** in `tests/test_defaults.py`:\n- `cli sub` with `{\"sub\": {\"opt\": 42}}` gives `42`.\n- Nested groups (`cli grp sub`) with `{\"grp\": {\"sub\": {\"opt\": 7}}}` give `7`.\n- A subcommand missing from the map falls back to the option's own default.\n- A group-level option set at the top level still works next to the nested entries.\n\nI could also add a `CHANGES.md` entry if you want one.\n\n**Check:** run `pytest tests/test_defaults.py tests/test_context.py tests/test_commands.py`, then the full `pytest`.\n\nThe plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\defaults-configured-through-default-map-compiled-abelson.md`. Tell me to go ahead and I'll make the change.",
